 test with Candida antigens shows 2 cm of induration at 48 hours. The time of onset of the disease is best explained by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"development of a viral infection."},{"label":"B","text":"exposure to rare bacteria."},{"label":"C","text":"a maturation defect in the thymus."},{"label":"D","text":"transplacental transfer of IgM antibodies."},{"label":"E","text":"loss of passive immunity from the mother."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3351d92968468504952cdd81fe3cc9ff897b6daa"},{"id":"q-06c296d28677","stem":"Complement is involved in the pathogenesis of each of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arthus reaction."},{"label":"B","text":"contact dermatitis."},{"label":"C","text":"erythroblastosis foetalis."},{"label":"D","text":"haemolytic transfusion ABO reaction."},{"label":"E","text":"serum sickness."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5dc8a4ec964c057471fc6e89c7927d1704c39957"},{"id":"q-13d367e0991d","stem":"Which of the fo