ly divide but proliferate in response to injury"},{"label":"E","text":"Cells that require the presence of growth factors for mitotic division"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e71211980b74e761dcf049d9e9a4f421fa7b9b9d"},{"id":"q-b728d65c591d","stem":"What are \"heart failure\" cells histologically seen in pulmonary edema?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hyperplasia of type II pneumocytes"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemosiderin laden macrophages"},{"label":"C","text":"Lipofuscin laden macrophages"},{"label":"D","text":"Hyperplasia of clara cells"},{"label":"E","text":"All the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-5ec9afa5cf9f","stem":"Psammoma bodies are seen in which neoplasm?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Astrocytoma"},{"label":"B","text":"Meningioma"},{"label":"C","text":"Glioblastoma multiforme"},{"label":"D","text":"Cranyopharyngioma"},{"label":"E","text":"Chordoma"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":