ction of LTB4 is to increase permeability."},{"label":"B","text":"PGE2 causes intense vasoconstriction."},{"label":"C","text":"permeability increase caused by LTD4 restricted to venules."},{"label":"D","text":"LTC4, LTD4, LTE4, are important vasodilators."},{"label":"E","text":"cyclo-oxygenase is the predominant enzyme in neutrophils. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Tissue response to injury SUBCATEGORY Acute inflammation SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 69 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 CORRECT RESPONSE C APPLICATION"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-87695020fbc7","stem":"Regarding complement FILE NUMBER ??.??.?? CORRECT RESPONSE D?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C5a is an important opsonising molecule."},{"label":"B","text":"C3b has chemotactic function."},{"label":"C","text":"it cannot cause cytolysis of bacteria in the absence of immune complexes."},{"label":"D","text":"C3a may cause mast cell degranulation."},{"label":"E","text":"may be activated by prostaglandins. SUBJECT Pathology SUBJECT CATEGORY Tissue response to injury SUBCATEGORY Acute inflammation SOURCE OF QUESTION TEXT Robbins EDITION 5th PAGE(s) 66-67 ORIGINATOR Masonic Hospital primary exam course DATE 1996 APPLICATION"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAns