nged due to = the=20 long half-life of factor VII"},{"label":"D","text":"factors II, VII, IX, and X are = not=20 activated (carboxylated) when warfarin is administered in = therapeutic=20 doses"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e8053230469f","stem":"= Drugs=20 which interact with warfarin to increase its anticoagulant=20 effect include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ranitidine"},{"label":"B","text":"= trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole"},{"label":"C","text":"=20 rifampin"},{"label":"D","text":"nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8a1291f12251","stem":"= The=20 mechanism of action of mini-dose heparin is correctly described = by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"=20 factor X is more sensitive to heparin than are other = serine protease=20 factors"},{"label":"B","text":"mini-dose heparin is useful prophylactically rather than = during active clot formation"},{"label":"C","text":"by inhibiting factor X = activation, a=20 relative block of the clotting cascade develops, with less thrombin = formed"},{"label":"D","text":"the major action is to directly inhibit factor II, which = is=20 very sensitive to heparin"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-315a14aca2bb","stem":"6em Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif; BACKGROUND: #777; COLOR: = #dadada !important; PADDING-TOP: 5px !important } #nav LI LI A:hover { COLOR: #fff !important } #nav LI LI A:active { COLOR: #fff !important } #nav LI.current_page_parent LI.current_page_item A:hover { COLOR: #fff !important } #nav LI.current_page_parent LI.current_page_item A:active { COLOR: #fff !important } #nav LI:hover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav LI LI:hover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav LI LI LI:hover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav LI.sfhover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav LI LI.sfhover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav LI LI LI.sfhover UL { LEFT: auto } #nav UL UL { MARGIN: 0px 0px 0px -4px } #nav-cat { POSITION: relative; PADDING-BOTTOM: 6px; LINE-HEIGHT: 1; MARGIN: 0px = auto; PADDING-LEFT: 15px; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px; BACKGROUND: #607b88; = BORDER-TOP: #83a8b9 1px solid; PADDING-TOP: 6px } #nav-cat LI { POSITION: relative; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0px !important; LIST-STYLE-TYPE: = none; PADDING-LEFT: 13px !important; PADDING-RIGHT: 10px !important; = FLOAT: left; LIST-STYLE-IMAGE: none; MARGIN-RIGHT: 10px; BORDER-RIGHT: = #83a8b9 1px dotted; PADDING-TOP: 0px !important } #nav-cat A { PADDING-BOTTOM: 3px; DISPLAY: block; FONT: bold 1em Arial, Verdana; = LETTER-SPACING: 0.07em; COLOR: #c6dce6; TEXT-DECORATION: none } #nav-cat A:visited { PADDING-BOTTOM: 3px; DISPLAY: block; FONT: bold 1em Arial, Verdana; = LETTER-SPACING: 0.07em; COLOR: #c6dce6; TEXT-DECORATION: none } #nav-c