swer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic","url_or_navigation_embedded"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6da354bd68fb","stem":"An AIDS patient, who is being treated with multiple drugs, develops breast hypertrophy, central adiposity, hyperlipidemia, insulin resistance and nephrolithiasis. If these changes are related to his drug t reatment, this drug belongs to which group of anti-retroviral drugs? A 35 year old HIV positive male patient comes to the OPD with complaint of anorexia, nausea and vomiting and abdominal pain. His abdomen is tender in the epigastric area. Laboratory results reveal a raised serum amylase activity and a preliminary dia gnosis is made of acute pancreatitis. Which of the following anti-retroviral drugs has the patient most likely been taking? eceiving HAART regimen (Highly active anti-retroviral therapy). Four weeks after initiating therapy, he comes to the emergency department complaining of severe pain in the flank, nausea and frequent urination. Which one of the following drugs is most like ly the cause of his symptoms? hes, irritability, and nightmares. Which one of the following anti-retroviral drugs is most likely to be causing these symptoms? is B infection and therapy is initiated. Just after a few hours she comes to the emergency department complaining of fever, chills and muscle aches. Which one of the following drugs most likely caused these symptoms?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors (NRTIS)"},{"label":"B","text":"Non-nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors (NNRTIS)"},{"label":"C","text":"Fusion Inhibitors"},{"label":"D","text":"Protease Inhibitors"},{"label":"E","text":"Integrase Inhibitors 2."},{"label":"A","text":"Saquinavir"},{"label":"B","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"C","text":"Didanosine"},{"label":"D","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"E","text":"Enfuvirtide 3. A 40 year old HIV positive patient is r"},{"label":"A","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"B","text":"Indinavir"},{"label":"C","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"D","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nelfinavir 4. A 30 year old man is recently diagnosed with HIV and therapy is started. After the first week of therapy, the patient complains of headac"},{"label":"A","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"B","text":"Indinavir"},{"label":"C","text":"Lamivudine"},{"label":"D","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"E","text":"Stavudine 5. A 35 year old woman is diagnosed with chronic hepatit"},{"label":"A","text":"Lamivudine"},{"label":"B","text":"Adefovir"},{"label":"C","text":"Entecavir"},{"label":"D","text":"Interferon alfa"},{"label":"E","text":"Ribavirin"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_labels","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5e9b462c37dc","stem":"A 60 year old man with known history of Parkinsons disease is to receive prophylaxis against Influenza A virus. He is given a drug that is useful against Parkinson s disease as well for prophylaxisagainst influenza. The drug with which of the following mechanisms of action is most likely to have been given?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It prevents entry and penetration of the virus"},{"label":"B","text":"It prevents uncoating of the virus"},{"label":"C","text":"It prevents replication of the virus"},{"label":"D","text":"It prevents assembly of newly synthesized virus particles"},{"label":"E","text":"It prevents release of the newly synthesized virus \\* PAGE 4"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b73364661b9f2d164df81bd1ead795f86c0f6fd9"},{"id":"q-69971c48e957","stem":"Which of the following statements abo ut antiviral drugs are correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unlike antibacterial drugs, resistance to antiviral drugs is negligible"},{"label":"B","text":"They are sometimes used in combination to improveclinical outcomes"},{"label":"C","text":"Several antiviral drugs are also active against some bacteria and protozoa"},{"label":"D","text":"Most antiviral drugs are able to eliminate both replicating and latent viruses"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverifie