patic first-pass metabolism of the drug (p. 8, 9)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a62938e88be3","stem":"5 In addition to slow intravenous infusion, which of the following routes of administration allows for titration of the dose of a drug with the response","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sublingual"},{"label":"B","text":"Transdermal"},{"label":"C","text":"Inhalational"},{"label":"D","text":"Nasal insufflation (p. 9)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c640cdfcf116","stem":"6 Which of the following drugs is administered by intra- nasal spray/application for systemic action","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phenylephrine"},{"label":"B","text":"Desmopressin"},{"label":"C","text":"Azelastine"},{"label":"D","text":"Beclomethasone dipropionate (p. 9, 540)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3f299103ecd7","stem":"7 Compared to subcutaneous injection, the intramus- cular injection of drugs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is more painful"},{"label":"B","text":"Produces faster response"},{"label":"C","text":"Is unsuitable for depot preparations"},{"label":"D","text":"Carries greater risk of anaphylactic reaction (p. 9, 10)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"90222e7a091c72df5518fab36e0eb01b68d9f6b7"},{"id":"q-ba960d618db3","stem":"8 Select the route of administration which carries the highest risk of adversely affecting vital functions","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Intra arterial injection"},{"label":"B","text":"Intrathecal injection"},{"label":"C","text":"Intravenous injection"},{"label":"D","text":"Intramuscular injection (p. 10)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-573e3cff94a3","stem":"1 Alkalinization of urine hastens the excretion of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Weakly basic drugs"},{"label":"B","text":"Weakly acidic drugs"},{"label":"C","text":"Strong electrolytes"},{"label":"D","text":"Nonpolar drugs (p. 13, 26)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1a80700cbf4b","stem":"2 Majority of drugs cross biological membranes primarily by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Passive diffusion"},{"label":"B","text":"Facilitated diffusion"},{"label":"C","text":"Active transport"},{"label":"D","text":"Pinocytosis (p. 12)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8c6cb79e2869","stem":"3 Diffusion of drugs across cell membrane","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is dependent upon metabolic activity of the cell"},{"label":"B","text":"Is competitively inhibited by chemically related drugs"},{"label":"C","text":"Is affected by extent of ionization of drug mole- cules"},{"label":"D","text":"Exhibits saturation kinetics (p. 12)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],